# Swift and SwiftUI

- Keep UI and SwiftData ModelContext mutation on `@MainActor`.
- Give every Task an owner and cancellation boundary; never repair races with fixed sleeps.
- Prefer system navigation, text selection, media pickers, Charts, speech, and HealthKit UI.
- Preserve the two-tab information architecture and move low-frequency controls into settings.
- Label editable values, expose destructive actions with system semantics, and support Dynamic Type.
- New files should stay below 500 lines; avoid expanding existing oversized files.
- Add deterministic tests for business rules and manual device notes for hardware-only behavior.
- Run `make format` and `make check`.
